    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen changing an option from inside an `ftplugin/*.lua` file or in a `FileType` autocommand, it does not seem to trigger the `OptionSet` event.\n\nNotes:\n- The example uses `autocmd FileType lua`, but the same happens when putting `vim.bo.shiftwidth=2` inside a file `ftplugin/lua.lua`\n- when putting the above line inside a `vim.schedule()`, the event `OptionSet` does get triggered correctly\n- inside `ftplugin/lua.lua`, calling `vim.in_fast_event()` returns `false`\n- inside `ftplugin/lua.lua`, the variable `vim.v.option_type` is `''`, from which I deduce that I'm not inside a recursive `set` situation\n- adding `++nested` to the `autocmd OptionSet` line does not solve the issue\n- motivation: I'm trying to automatically adjust `listchars.leadmultispace` whenever `shiftwidth` changes. This typically happens when switching between file types due to different indentation conventions.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n`nvim --clean`, then:\n```vim\n:autocmd! FileType lua setl sw=2\n:autocmd! OptionSet shiftwidth setl lcs+=leadmultispace:-+\n:edit init.lua\n:set lcs?\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe last line should show `listchars=leadmultispace:-+`\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.11.1\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nyes, vim 9.1.1275\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nFedora 42\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.41.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nsystem package manager",
