            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I don't think this is a bug, but rather an (in this case) unfortunate consequence of intentional behaviour.\n\nFiletype detection and its configuration runs through autocmds (all are part of the `filetypedetect` autocmd-group). I've found autcmds for some events cannot trigger OptionSet unless they are marked as `nested` and that includes `BufReadPost` `StdInReadPost` and `BufNewFile` (which are the commands in the `filetypedetect` augroup) and `FileType`.\n\nIn your example, if you add the `++nested` flag to the `FileType` autocmd, then the `OptionSet` autocmd *will* fire.\n\nSo unfortunately, it is not possible to detect options set under certain autocommands unless those autocommands have been explicitly marked with `nested`, which isnnot the default.",
